window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>MEET DR KATE HANSON. SHE’S A FORENSIC PSYCHOLOGIST WHO GETS INTO THE MINDS OF THE WORST KILLERS IMAGINABLE.<br> <br> Two teenage boys make a gruesome discovery. A body locked inside a church crypt. The victim’s throat viciously ripped out.<br> <br> The dead man is quickly identified as twenty-year-old Matthew Flynn, son of a wealthy businessman. He was reported missing a year ago.<br> <br> Nothing about the crime scene makes sense to forensic psychologist Kate Hanson. The evidence reveals careful planning — but also a frenzied loss of control. Kate and her team disagree about the killer’s motive — is it drugs? Money? Sex?<br> <br> Then another young man’s remains are found. Someone who knew Matthew. And the case takes an even darker turn . . .</p>"; 
